course: dictionary
lesson: 7750
title: A word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pundit is an expert who often gives opinions on TV, on the radio or in newspapers. When you hear «football pundits» on TV, they are the experts who explain what happened in the match. The clues are the TV, the match and the opinions they share.
explain: Pundit has a second meaning too. In Hinduism, a pundit (also spelled pandit) is a learned teacher or priest. The sentence «From Sanskrit, the ancient language of India, came "guru" (teacher), "pundit" (learned person) and "avatar"» gives you the clue: the brackets tell you that a pundit is a learned person.
explain: A pundit gives opinions, and an opinion is not always a fact. Ask yourself: can I check this? When political pundits disagree, read more than one view and compare them before you decide what you think.
fact: A pundit is an expert who gives opinions on TV, on the radio or in newspapers.
fact: «Pundit» can also mean a learned teacher or priest in Hinduism.
fact: Pundits often talk about football and politics.
fact: An opinion is what someone thinks, and a fact is something that can be checked.
fact: From Sanskrit, the ancient language of India, came «pundit» (learned person), «guru» (teacher) and «avatar».
exercise: «Football pundits explained the goal on TV.» What is a pundit? | A kind of football boot | A TV camera operator | A player who scores goals | *An expert who gives opinions on TV, on the radio or in newspapers
exercise: «In the temple, the pundit read from the old holy book.» What is a pundit here? | A kind of drum | A visitor who has never read a book | A shop that sells books | *A learned teacher or priest
exercise: «From Sanskrit, the ancient language of India, came "pundit".» Find and copy the word that tells you Sanskrit is very old. | language | *ancient | India | came
test: A pundit says the team will win. What should you do before you believe it? | Ask the pundit to pay for your ticket | Ignore all sport forever | *Check the facts and compare what other experts say | Believe it, because pundits are always right
test: «The learned pundit taught the children the old stories.» What does pundit mean in this sentence? | *A learned teacher | A football expert | A type of old story | A newspaper reporter
exam: Which is the plural of pundit? | pundit's | pundites | *pundits | punditing
